      "id": "hackernews-2026-05-19-cursor-cloud-agents-down",
      "title": "Cursor Cloud Agents Down",
      "summary": "Article URL: https://forum.cursor.com/t/cloud-agents-broken-ii/161036\nComments URL: https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=48196479\nPoints: 7\n# Comments: 1",
      "body": "Where does the bug appear (feature/product)?\nBackground Agent (GitHub, Slack, Web, Linear)\nCloud agents are failing to spin up today, they were working just fine yesterday. I started multiple sessions and have been waiting 10+ minutes for them to start.\nStart a conversation with a cloud agent.\nThe conversation with the cloud agent starts\nFor AI issues: which model did you use?\nDoes this stop you from using Cursor\nYes - Cursor is unusable\nThanks for the update, @deanrie , we can close out as a duplicate.\nMinor feedback, but the “all systems operational” banner at the top is misleading. It would be nice to have known incidents at the top of the page versus the bottom.\nThanks for the feedback on the status page, that’s fair. Having the green All Systems Operational at the top while there’s an active incident below does look contradictory. I’ll pass this on to the team that owns the page.\nYou can track progress for the incident here: Cursor Status - Degraded behavior in cloud agents and automations.",
